# Common Ground design language

Keep this permanent. Super simple: **black background, white CMU Serif, film grain**.

## Must use

- **Typography:** Computer Modern / CMU Serif for UI text; CMU Typewriter Text for monospace (codes, timer). Import via `computer-modern` in `src/index.css`. Never Inter, Roboto, system-ui, or other default sans stacks.
- **Texture:** Film grain is applied on `body::before` in `src/index.css` (fine grit, light screen blend). Do not remove it. Keep cards borderless / transparent on the black field.
- **Tokens:** All colors, fonts, and shared element styles live in `src/theme.ts`. Prefer those tokens; do not invent a parallel palette.
- **Styling format:** Inline `style={{ ... }}` objects only (no Tailwind, no CSS modules for components).

## Visual rules

- Black field (`color.bg` ≈ `#000000`), white text (`color.text`), muted gray for secondary copy.
- **No all-caps styling** — no `textTransform: 'uppercase'`, no letterspaced kickers/labels. Sentence case everywhere (including spectrum labels and win/lose).
- Square corners (`borderRadius: 0`). No bordered cards on auth/onboarding.
- Primary buttons: white fill, black text. Secondary: transparent with a quiet border.
- No gradients, glow effects, soft drop shadows, warm cream paper, or purple SaaS themes.
- Party blue/red (`color.left` / `color.right`) only on the results spectrum, at equal weight.

## When changing UI

Match this language. Do not reintroduce newsprint cream, amber accents, or all-caps rubrics.
